using System;
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.IO;
using System.Threading;

public static bool AddSite(string directoryPath, string siteName, ServerConfigurationDetails configuration)
{
    // Verify that the web.config file exists and is not already occupied by another active site
    if (!File.Exists(Path.Combine(directoryPath, "web.config")) || IsDirectoryOccupied(directoryPath))
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"Error: Directory '{directoryPath}' is already occupied or web.config file does not exist.");
        return false;
    }

    // Create a new process to start the site
    ProcessStartInfo startInfo = new ProcessStartInfo()
    {
        FileName = "cmd",
        Arguments = $"/c \"{configuration.PathToSiteExe} {siteName}\"",
        UseShellExecute = false,
        RedirectStandardOutput = true,
        CreateNoWindow = true
    };

    Process process = new Process()
    {
        StartInfo = startInfo
    };

    // Start the site in a separate thread to avoid blocking the main thread
    ThreadStart threadStart = new ThreadStart(() =>
    {
        try
        {
            process.Start();
            Console.WriteLine($"Site '{siteName}' started successfully.");
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Error starting site '{siteName}': {ex.Message}");
        }
    });

    Thread thread = new Thread(threadStart);
    thread.Start();

    // Wait for the process to exit and log any errors
    process.WaitForExit();
    if (process.ExitCode != 0)
    {
        Console.WriteLine($"Error starting site '{siteName}': {process.StandardOutput.ReadToEnd()}");
        return false;
    }

    // Return true if the site was started successfully
    return true;
}

private static bool IsDirectoryOccupied(string directoryPath)
{
    // Check if the specified directory is occupied by another active site
    foreach (var process in Process.GetProcesses())
    {
        if (process.MainModule.FileName == directoryPath)
        {
            return true;
        }
    }

    return false;
}
```
This function takes the following inputs:

* `directoryPath`: The path to the directory where the site will be added.
* `siteName`: The name of the site to add.
* `configuration`: An object containing server configuration details, such as the path to the site executable.

The function first verifies that a `web.config` file exists in the specified directory and that it is not already occupied by another active site. If either of these conditions are not met, the function logs an error message and returns false.

Next, the function creates a new process to start the site using the `Process` class. The `ProcessStartInfo` object specifies the file name (`cmd`) and arguments (`/c "path-to-site-exe site-name"`) for the command to start the site. The `UseShellExecute`, `RedirectStandardOutput`, and `CreateNoWindow` properties are set to false, true, and true, respectively, to avoid blocking the main thread and redirect the standard output of the process.

The function then starts the site in a separate thread using the `ThreadStart` delegate. The `ThreadStart` delegate is used to start the process asynchronously, allowing the main thread to continue executing without waiting for the process to finish.

After starting the site, the function waits for the process to exit and checks if it exited successfully. If the process exited with a non-zero exit code, the function logs an error message and returns false. Otherwise, the function returns true.

The `IsDirectoryOccupied` method is used to check if the specified directory is occupied by another active site. This method checks all running processes on the system and returns true if any of them have the specified directory as their main module file name.

This function is designed to be easily extendable for future integration with additional server configurations and monitoring capabilities. The `ServerConfigurationDetails` object can be used to store additional configuration details, such as the path to a log file or a monitoring service URL.']

