The `add_item` function takes a pointer to the head of the list as input, and adds a new item to the end of the list. If the list is empty, it sets the head pointer to the new item. Otherwise, it adds the new item to the end of the list by traversing the list until it finds the last item, and then setting its `next` pointer to the new item.

