This implementation uses a dynamic array to store the tasks, which allows for efficient addition and deletion of tasks. The `addTask` function checks if the list is full before adding a new task, and if it is, it doubles the capacity of the list to accommodate more tasks. The `updateTask` function updates the task at the specified index by freeing the old name and replacing it with the new one. The `deleteTask` function shifts all tasks after the specified index to fill the gap, and then decrements the size of the list. The `findTaskByName` function iterates over all tasks and compares their names with the specified name, returning the index of the first match or -1 if no match is found. The `sortTasksByPriority` and `sortTasksByDeadline` functions use bubble sort algorithms to sort the tasks by priority and deadline respectively. Finally, the `printTasks` function iterates over all tasks and prints their details.

