This code defines a data structure to store tasks and records, with efficient insertion, deletion, and retrieval operations. The data structure is thread-safe, allowing multiple threads to access and modify it simultaneously without race conditions or data corruption. The function to add a new task allocates memory for the new task and adds it to the end of an array, while the function to update an existing task updates the priority and status of the corresponding task in the array. The function to retrieve tasks based on their priority finds all tasks with the given priority and returns them as an array. The function to add a new record to the linked list allocates memory for the new record and adds it to the end of a linked list, while the function to delete a record from the linked list finds the record with the given value and deletes it from the linked list. The functions to serialize and deserialize the data structure to and from a file use a custom binary format optimized for performance and include compression to reduce file size while maintaining data integrity. The function to free the memory allocated for the data structure frees all memory allocated for the tasks and records, as well as sets the number of tasks and records to 0.']

