The `processFile` function takes a filename as input and processes it by reading its contents into a string, creating a new instance of the `JsonObject` class from the file contents, and incrementing line count and character count based on the contents of the JSON object. The `processFiles` function takes a vector of filenames as input and processes each one in parallel using multi-threading. It also generates a comprehensive report of aggregated line counts and total character counts across all specified files.

