This code implements the given programming task by reading an XML file containing an array of script objects and processing each object line by line. It dynamically allocates memory to store the content of each script object, computes the average of the last two fields, and appends this average as the last field in a comma-separated format. The program also handles objects with varying lengths and complex data types, including integers, strings, and booleans, stored in a dynamic data structure. It ensures thread safety and avoids race conditions by implementing appropriate synchronization mechanisms. Additionally, it monitors and alerts the system administrator if memory usage exceeds a predefined threshold. The program handles edge cases such as zero-sized input parameters and potential memory overflow during dynamic resizing. It also gracefully handles memory allocation failures, ensuring the application remains in a consistent state. Finally, it renders the processed script objects as a footer of a web page, converting each object into a <script> tag with a key and innerHTML set to the script's code. The function returns a single, concatenated string representing all the script tags.']

